    "body": "## Compatibility\n\n**IntelEngine 3.5.2 requires SkyrimNet Beta 25 or newer. It is not compatible with SkyrimNet Beta 24 or earlier.**\n\nThis update improves Skyrim SE/AE compatibility. Tested on Skyrim 1.6.1170, with Epicrob also confirming success on his affected 1.7.x setup. Use matching SKSE and Address Library; this build does not support VR.\n\nIntelEngine was originally created by [Galanx](https://github.com/galanx). Thanks to [Epicrob](https://github.com/epicrob99) for the compatibility PR, compiler-flag guidance, and 1.7.x testing.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Uses pinned MinLL/CommonLibVR with the audited non-VR ABI correction.\n- Rebuilds the native DLL using VS 2022 and the corrected compiler flags, retaining C++23 support.\n- Includes the freshly compiled Papyrus scripts and rebuilt dashboard in the full package.\n- Preserves the tested DLL and runtime payload byte-for-byte. Release/installer version is 3.5.2; the native DLL continues to report 3.5.1.\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload `IntelEngine-v3.5.2.zip` and install it with Mod Organizer 2. Replace the previous IntelEngine installation; do not enable multiple IntelEngine versions together.\n\nSHA-256: `2c827385fc23f98a81be48a75ceb30c414963c832bdf69432cd6f519d682db37`\n\nExisting Papyrus/translation cleanup remains tracked separately. This release does not claim to fix CTD issue #15 or establish every Skyrim patch/task scenario.\n\n[Native source for this release](https://github.com/Gerkinfeltser/IntelEngine-NativePlugin/tree/v3.5.2)\n",
